# Extensions production's PGDATA actually contains — #2661.
#
# This file is the EXPECTATION the monthly restore drill asserts against. It
# exists because `deploy/postgres/Dockerfile`'s package list is a claim about
# what a restore needs, and nothing checked it: #974 moved the base image off
# expired bullseye and installed the two packages the product uses explicitly,
# correctly — and with that silently stopped supplying
# `postgis_tiger_geocoder`, which the old `postgis/postgis` base had bundled.
# The repo's database image then could not restore the production backup for
# five weeks, with every check green, because the only thing that reads the
# package set against production's real catalogue is the drill, and it runs
# monthly.
#
# MEASURED on agrent_production, 2026-11-07, owner-authorised read-only query:
#
#   SELECT extname, extversion FROM pg_extension ORDER BY extname;
#
# Not inferred from the Dockerfile. The Dockerfile installs two packages; the
# cluster carries SEVEN extensions, and the gap is the whole defect — three of
# these arrive as dependencies or as part of a bundle rather than by explicit
# intent, which is exactly how one of them went missing without anyone
# choosing to remove it.
#
# One name per line, `#` comments ignored. Versions are deliberately NOT pinned
# here: a minor extension bump is routine and pinning would make the drill fail
# on an upgrade that is fine. The property is PRESENCE — a restore that cannot
# create an extension fails with an opaque pg_restore error, and that is what
# this turns into a named comparison.
#
# Adding a line is a claim that production needs it. Removing one is a claim
# that it does not, and `postgis_tiger_geocoder` is exactly that question —
# tracked on #2662, which proposes dropping it from production first and the
# package second. Do NOT drop the line here before the extension is gone from
# production, or the drill starts asserting a set production does not have.

fuzzystrmatch
pg_trgm
plpgsql
postgis
postgis_tiger_geocoder
postgis_topology
vector
